WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.300
Inventa: decentralized, self-improving agents for autonomous scientific discovery.

2
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.956
Language model agents can generate research ideas,

3
00:00:10.006 --> 00:00:11.941
and refine them through experiments.

4
00:00:11.991 --> 00:00:16.793
But adding more agents, or more iterations, does not automatically produce more diverse,

5
00:00:16.843 --> 00:00:18.116
or more feasible, ideas.

6
00:00:18.166 --> 00:00:22.912
Agents converge on similar candidates, spread unsupported claims through shared memory,

7
00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:26.330
and keep applying search strategies that have stopped working.

8
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.059
Inventa draws on how science advances in practice.

9
00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:32.548
Research groups pursue different approaches,

10
00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.150
while building on evidence reported by others.

11
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.610
Prior methods range from repeated sampling,

12
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.003
to island-based evolution with fixed, partially adaptive,

13
00:00:42.053 --> 00:00:43.550
or centralized strategies,

14
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.872
and all of them keep the mutator fixed.

15
00:00:45.922 --> 00:00:50.991
In Inventa, each decentralized unit has a local orchestrator that evolves its mutator,

16
00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:53.670
while only verifiers publish shared findings.

17
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:59.655
A research task comes with a question, a workspace of literature, tools and data,

18
00:00:59.705 --> 00:01:01.790
domain constraints, and verifiers.

19
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.831
Inventa runs many autonomous research units in parallel.

20
00:01:05.881 --> 00:01:09.210
Each unit is like a lab, with its own lineage of ideas.

21
00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.670
In every round, a unit reads a snapshot of the shared knowledge,

22
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.083
and selects a parent from its idea tree.

23
00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.556
Its mutator agent, the junior researcher,

24
00:01:18.606 --> 00:01:21.330
then revises the parent into a new child idea.

25
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.967
Verifiers test the child on data the mutator never sees.

26
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:29.847
They score it on held-out data, check the domain constraints, test it out of distribution,

27
00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:31.257
and ablate its components,

28
00:01:31.307 --> 00:01:34.890
and they return a certificate with the evidence behind every check.

29
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.126
Only verifiers write to the shared knowledge:

30
00:01:38.176 --> 00:01:41.406
verified improvements, partial components worth reusing,

31
00:01:41.456 --> 00:01:43.983
and refuted ideas that violate a constraint.

32
00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.150
It is the only channel between units.

33
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.909
The unit accepts the child only if any extra complexity buys fitness,

34
00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:52.657
and records it in its memory.

35
00:01:52.707 --> 00:01:55.370
Rejected children stay, as negative evidence.

36
00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.387
An orchestrator, the lab's principal investigator, adapts the search itself.

37
00:02:00.437 --> 00:02:04.629
It retools the mutator's harness when a twin trial shows fitter children,

38
00:02:04.679 --> 00:02:06.605
redraws a better model on a stall,

39
00:02:06.655 --> 00:02:10.440
and restarts with a new research direction when the stall repeats.

40
00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:16.073
Across five benchmarks spanning the research cycle, Inventa leads every one.

41
00:02:16.123 --> 00:02:19.747
On EurekaBench, it reaches seventy-three point six percent,

42
00:02:19.797 --> 00:02:22.113
against fifty-six point two for CORAL,

43
00:02:22.163 --> 00:02:26.535
and it is the only method that passes every scientific constraint test.

44
00:02:26.585 --> 00:02:30.022
On IdeaBench, it finds twenty-six novel ideas per paper,

45
00:02:30.072 --> 00:02:32.824
against eighteen point six for ResearchAgent,

46
00:02:32.874 --> 00:02:35.440
with eighty-two percent fewer model calls.

47
00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.714
And it keeps improving as the budget grows,

48
00:02:38.764 --> 00:02:41.860
while frontier agents and evolutionary methods level off.

49
00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.496
Take one discovery, on Milky-Way-mass halos.

50
00:02:45.546 --> 00:02:47.983
The textbook law, adiabatic contraction,

51
00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:52.833
assumes that dark matter falls inward with the full pull of the stars and gas,

52
00:02:52.883 --> 00:02:55.196
and it overshoots the central density.

53
00:02:55.246 --> 00:02:58.864
Inventa found that dark matter responds only about halfway,

54
00:02:58.914 --> 00:03:02.595
and that the galaxy, not the halo's mass, sets how strongly.

55
00:03:02.645 --> 00:03:07.134
At the centre, its law lands about three times closer to the simulations.

56
00:03:07.184 --> 00:03:10.119
On this task it scores seventy-five point eight,

57
00:03:10.169 --> 00:03:13.290
against fifty-two point four for the best baseline.

58
00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.540
Inventa. Decentralized, self-improving agents for autonomous scientific discovery.
